   "wanted": "A figure of any face but the front, which on this device is a smaller hole than usual and is worth saying why. The datasheet's key features include \"All ports, PSUs and fan modules are front access\" and \"Maintenance activity to replace PSUs and FANs can be done from the front panel without remove the product from rack\" - so the rear carries no user hardware at all. The quick start's callout 11 is a \"Grounding screw\"; it is not located, so it is not placed. The SIDE panels carry the intake and exhaust on a side-to-side box and no figure shows either. Per docs/deliberately-empty-faces.md these faces are DECLARED empty with the reason rather than left silent, which is the difference between empty-by-verification and empty-by-omission.",
